LibreHardwareMonitorLib — Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
https://github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor
================================================================================

SysScope ships a native DLL (`src-tauri/resources/sysscope_sensors.dll`) that is
compiled from `sensor-bridge/` and statically links LibreHardwareMonitorLib via
.NET NativeAOT. It is used to read CPU/GPU temperatures, CPU package power, per-
core clocks, core voltage and storage SMART data.

MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft license. The source of the bridge that consumes
it is in this repository under `sensor-bridge/`. If you modify
LibreHardwareMonitorLib itself, you must make those modified files available
under MPL-2.0. A copy of the license is available at:
https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/

Note: reading low-level sensors requires a kernel driver that this library loads
at runtime; this is why SysScope requests administrator privileges.

